WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你们录制了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们将剖析《办公室》的一集，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能讲述的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.920
Hey, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.460
Hi, you guys.
嗨，大家好。

10
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:36.940
This week, we are talking about The Convict, Season 3, Episode 9, written by Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
本周，我们要讨论的是《罪犯》，第三季第九集，由瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特编剧，杰弗里·布里茨执导。

11
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.060
There's some powerhouse there.
阵容非常强大。

12
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

13
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:40.820
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

14
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.380
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

15
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:41.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

16
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.960
Well, I'm wasting no time.
好吧，我废话不多说。

17
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.580
I'm going to hit you with a summary.
我要直接给你们讲讲剧情梗概。

18
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.980
Hit me, baby, one more time.
再来一次，宝贝。

19
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.320
Oh, baby, baby.
哦，宝贝，宝贝。

20
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.280
Just give me a summary.
快给我讲讲梗概吧。

21
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.300
Oh, my God.
我的天哪。

22
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.620
Oh, Brittany, we love you.
哦，布兰妮，我们爱你。

23
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.200
All right.
好吧。

24
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:04.600
In this episode, Michael learns that one of the new Stanford transfers, Martin Nash, is a reformed convict.
在本集中，迈克尔得知新来的斯坦福转校生马丁·纳什是一个改过自新的罪犯。

25
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:12.400
When Martin tells the other employees about his time in prison, the staff says it sounds like it's better than working at Dunder Mifflin.
当马丁向其他员工讲述他在监狱的经历时，大家说听起来比在邓德·米夫林工作还要好。

26
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.660
Well, Michael is heartbroken to hear that people would rather be in prison than at Dunder Mifflin.
好吧，迈克尔听到人们宁愿坐牢也不愿意在邓德·米夫林工作，心碎不已。

27
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:25.420
So, he responds by turning into prison Mike to scare them all straight.
于是，他摇身一变成为“监狱迈克”，试图把他们吓回正道。

28
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.920
And then also, Andy asks Jim for advice on how to woo Pam.
与此同时，安迪向吉姆征求如何追求帕姆的建议。

29
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.680
And we get a little bit of a prank.
我们还会看到一个小恶作剧。

30
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.020
He's going to woo Pam.
他要去追求帕姆。

31
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.700
There's going to be some banjo playing.
会有一些班卓琴演奏。

32
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:36.980
It's real special.
非常特别。

33
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.000
Jenna, I know you're about to hit me with some fast facts, but I bet I can't guess two of them.
珍娜，我知道你接下来要抛出一些快讯，但我敢说我能猜中其中两个。

34
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.280
Hit you with some fast facts.
给你来点快讯。

35
00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.380
Oh, no.
哦，不。

36
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:48.580
Oh, no.
哦，不。

37
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.100
This is bad.
这可不妙。

38
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.700
People right now are hitting fast forward.
现在大家都在按快进。

39
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.960
They're like, please, can I skip past them doing Britney Spears?
他们会想，求求了，我能跳过她们模仿小甜甜布兰妮吗？

40
00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:01.420
Is your first fast fact that Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant created the office for the BBC?
你的第一个快讯是不是瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特为BBC创作了《办公室》？

41
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.420
They're the OG of the OG.
他们是鼻祖中的鼻祖。

42
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.300
Yes, Angela.
是的，安吉拉。

43
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.240
It is.
正是如此。

44
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.100
Yes.
没错。

45
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.200
And also, this is the only episode of The American Office that was written by Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant.
而且，这也是美版《办公室》中唯一一集由瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特编剧的剧集。

46
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.680
I didn't know that.
我不知道这件事。

47
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:21.720
Well, our pilot was sort of technically written by them because we really, we used so much of it.
好吧，我们的试播集从某种技术层面上讲也是他们写的，因为我们确实借鉴了太多内容。

48
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.260
But it was also adapted by Greg Daniels.
但它也是由格雷格·丹尼尔斯改编的。

49
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.940
But this is the only original American Office that they wrote.
不过这是他们编写的唯一一集原创美版《办公室》。

50
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.760
Now, Stephen did direct an episode.
话说回来，斯蒂芬确实导演过一集。

51
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.180
He directed Customer Survey in season five.
他在第五季时执导了《客户调查》。

52
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.720
And Ricky did a cameo in season seven.
里奇还在第七季里客串过。

53
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.140
And they were around.
而且他们经常在附近。

54
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.600
They would come visit us.
他们会来看望我们。

55
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.540
They would pop in.
他们会突然出现。

56
00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.440
I remember Stephen Merchant being in the writer's room a lot.
我记得斯蒂芬·莫切特经常待在编剧室里。

57
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:45.980
Yeah.
对。

58
00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.800
He would come by whenever he was in America.
他只要来美国就会顺便过来。

59
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.100
And you know, Angela, I did a movie with Stephen Merchant.
你知道吗，安吉拉，我和斯蒂芬·莫切特合作过一部电影。

60
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.780
You did a movie with the tall man from England?
你跟那个来自英国的高个子男人拍了电影？

61
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:53.740
Yes.
是的。

62
00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.360
It was called Hall Pass.
片名叫《放假通行证》。

63
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:55.940
Oh.
哦。

64
00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.000
And it was a Farrelly Brothers movie.
那是法雷利兄弟的电影。

65
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.000
It shot in Atlanta.
在亚特兰大拍摄的。

66
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.880
And I was so happy that Stephen Merchant was on this movie because this movie had like these huge powerhouse comedic stars.
我当时特别高兴斯蒂芬·莫切特也参演了这部电影，因为片中有很多那种超级大牌的喜剧明星。

67
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.400
OK, it was Owen Wilson.
好吧，有欧文·威尔逊。

68
00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.920
There was Jason Sudeikis, J.B.
有杰森·苏戴奇斯、J.B.

69
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.380
Smoove, Christina Applegate.
·斯穆夫、克里斯蒂娜·艾伯盖特。

70
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.060
And then like me.
然后就是像我这样的人。

71
00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.020
I remember I remember you going off to do this and you were like, oh, my God, I'm so nervous.
我记得，我记得你当时要去拍这部电影，然后你说，天哪，我好紧张。

72
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:21.620
I'm so nervous.
我太紧张了。

73
00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:21.700
Yes.
是的。

74
00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.980
I was so happy that I knew someone.
我很高兴能认识一个人。

75
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:24.400
Yeah.
对。

76
00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:30.800
So I kind of glommed on to Stephen Merchant when we were on that set because I was like someone I know.
所以在那个片场时，我有点像粘上了斯蒂芬·莫切特，因为我想，总算有个我认识的人了。

77
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:37.640
Because otherwise, when you go do those movies, I always feel like the new kid in school where it's like, where do I fit in?
因为平时你去拍那些电影时，我总是觉得自己像个转学生，心想，我该融入哪里呢？

78
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.000
I don't know anyone.
我谁也不认识。

79
00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:39.780
Yeah.
是啊。

80
00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.880
I was so nervous.
我当时紧张极了。

81
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.720
But there was another reason why I was very nervous on this movie.
但我在这部电影里感到非常紧张，还有另一个原因。

82
00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.200
And it was because I was staying in a haunted hotel.
那就是我住进了一家闹鬼的酒店。

83
00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:47.440
What?
什么？

84
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:47.540
What?
什么？

85
00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.060
Yes.
是的。

86
00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.160
You remember this?
你还记得这事吗？

87
00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:50.960
No.
不记得。

88
00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.320
Lady.
天呐。

89
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:53.600
Yes.
是的。

90
00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.380
I got to Atlanta and they put me up in this hotel.
我到了亚特兰大，他们把我安排在这家酒店。

91
00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:03.700
I would get woken up in the middle of the night at like 2.30 in the morning by the sound of clompy footsteps on my ceiling.
我会在半夜两点半左右被天花板上沉重的脚步声吵醒。

92
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.860
Well, that happens in hotels, lady.
得了吧，住酒店经常会这样，大姐。

93
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.460
Does it happen when your hotel room is on the top floor and there's nothing above you?
难道当你的酒店房间在顶楼、上面什么都没有的时候，也会这样吗？

94
00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.180
Does it?
会吗？

95
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.300
No.
不会。

96
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.960
I was on the top floor.
我住在顶楼。

97
00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:23.040
So I called down to the front desk and I was like, excuse me, do you guys do maintenance on the roof at like 2.30 in the morning?
所以我给前台打电话说，打扰一下，你们会在凌晨两点半左右在屋顶进行维修吗？

98
00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.400
Are people walking on the roof?
有人在屋顶上走动吗？

99
00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:25.240
What?
什么？

100
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.820
Well, the person on the phone was like, no.
电话那头的人说，没有。

101
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:34.900
And also, just because you're on the top floor, they're like, that doesn't mean that like your ceiling is literally the roof of the building.
而且，就算你住在顶楼，他们也会说，这并不意味着你的天花板字面意义上就是整栋大楼的屋顶。

102
00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.240
Like there's stuff in between the ceiling of your hotel.
就好像你酒店的天花板上面还有别的东西。

103
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.920
Like a secret floor?
就像一个秘密楼层？

104
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.760
That's what I said.
我也是这么说的。

105
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.120
Yes.
没错。

106
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.440
I said, what's happening there?
我说，那上面在发生什么？

107
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.280
Like when you get in an elevator and there's no button for it?
就像你坐电梯时发现根本没有那个楼层的按键一样？

108
00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.260
Yes.
对。

109
00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.720
That's what I wanted to know.
这就是我想知道的。

110
00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.460
What is happening in this space?
这个空间里到底在发生什么？

111
00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.780
Something is happening.
里面肯定有什么在发生。

112
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.580
People are walking.
有人在走动。

113
00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.160
Angela, I wouldn't let it go.
安吉拉，我要是你就绝不会罢休。

114
00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.060
Well, of course not.
那当然。

115
00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.540
So I went to a travel website and I Googled this hotel.
于是我上了一个旅游网站，在谷歌上搜了这家酒店。

116
00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.320
You did a deep dive on the hotel.
你对这家酒店进行了深入的人肉搜索。

117
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.820
It's a haunted hotel.
这是一家闹鬼的酒店。

118
00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:07.680
Oh, no.
噢，不会吧。

119
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:13.000
There were tons of stories of people who had stayed on the top floor who had heard the footsteps.
有大量的故事说，住在顶楼的人听到过脚步声。

120
00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.300
Shut the front door.
我的天哪。

121
00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:15.560
Okay.
好吧。

122
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.760
So now I can't sleep, right?
所以现在我睡不着了，对吧？

123
00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.520
Because you have a full on ghoSt.
因为你遇到了货真价实的鬼魂。

124
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.920
I'm in a ghost hotel.
我住进了一家鬼酒店。

125
00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.000
I have to go to work tomorrow with Owen Wilson.
我明天还要和欧文·威尔逊一起去工作。

126
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.580
I'm sleepless.
我失眠了。

127
00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.540
I'm nervous.
我很紧张。

128
00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.040
I called Lee crying in the middle of the night.
我半夜给李打着电话哭。

129
00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.820
Lee, who was my boyfriend at the time, who's back in Los Angeles writing a script.
李是我当时的男朋友，他当时在洛杉矶写剧本。

130
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.880
I was like, you need to fly here and you have to come keep me safe from the ghosts.
我说，你得飞到这儿来，你得来保护我免受鬼魂侵害。

131
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.680
You have to stay with me during this movie.
拍这部电影期间你得跟我住在一起。

132
00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.480
And he's like, what am I, a ghostbuster?
他说，我算什么，捉鬼敢死队吗？

133
00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:44.460
What the heck?
搞什么鬼？

134
00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.780
Jenna, just move hotels.
珍娜，直接换个酒店不就行了。

135
00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.380
That's what Lee said.
李是这么说的。

136
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.840
But I was like, I am not about to call this production company and insist that they move
但我心想，我才不要打电话给制片公司，坚持要求他们

137
00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:55.040
me from this hotel because it's haunted.
给我换酒店，就因为这里闹鬼。

138
00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.760
They would think you were Looney Tunes.
他们会觉得你是个疯子。

139
00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:02.740
They would be like, oh, this actress is convinced her hotel room is haunted and she wants to
他们会想，天哪，这个女演员确信她的酒店房间闹鬼，然后她想要

140
00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:03.060
move.
搬走。

141
00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:03.660
I get it.
我懂。

142
00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.160
I get it.
我懂的。

143
00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.940
So Lee flew out.
所以李真的飞过来了。

144
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.660
He stayed with me while I shot that movie and protected me from the ghoSt.
我拍那部电影期间他一直陪着我，保护我免受鬼魂侵害。

145
00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.560
And by the way, when he got there, he heard it.
顺便说一句，他到那儿的时候，他也听到了。

146
00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.500
He heard it.
他听到了。

147
00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.960
I would be so freaked out.
我要是遇到这事非吓死不可。

148
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.320
Well, oh my gosh, that fast fact took a turn.
天哪，那个冷知识真是来了个大反转。

149
00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:19.060
But I like that.
不过我喜欢这个。

150
00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.020
It really did.
确实如此。

151
00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.260
I'm here for it.
我太支持了。

152
00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:24.780
I'm going to steer us back onto the episode with fast fact number two.
我要把话题拉回到第二个快速冷知识上。

153
00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:29.220
This was the first episode directed by Jeff Blitz.
这是杰夫·布里茨执导的第一集。

154
00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.880
We love Jeff Blitz.
我们超爱杰夫·布里茨。

155
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.540
He directed 11 episodes of The Office.
他执导过11集《办公室》。

156
00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.380
This was his firSt.
这是他的第一集。

157
00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.740
He is a wonderful, delightful human being.
他是一个非常棒、非常讨人喜欢的人。

158
00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.320
I adore him.
我超级崇拜他。

159
00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:46.140
We reached out to Jeff and he sent in audio clips about this episode.
我们联系了杰夫，他发来了关于这一集的音频片段。

160
00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.160
We're so excited.
我们太兴奋了。

161
00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:52.040
I also told him I really need him to come back on because we need to discuss Save Bandit.
我还告诉他，我真的很需要他再来一次，因为我们需要讨论“救救小班迪特”。

162
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:52.460
Yes.
没错。

163
00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.980
And when I when I threw that cat in the ceiling, that has to be talked about.
而且当我把那只猫扔进天花板时，这必须得好好聊聊。

164
00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.140
Because he directed that episode, too, right?
因为那一集也是他导的，对吧？

165
00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:58.800
Yes.
是的。

166
00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.640
But you guys, I want to give a shout out to a movie that Jeff had done.
不过大家伙儿，我想向杰夫拍过的一部电影致敬。

167
00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.060
I had watched this movie.
我看过这部电影。

168
00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:04.820
It's a documentary.
这是一部纪录片。

169
00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:08.680
I was a huge fan of it and a fan of his.
我是它的超级粉丝，也是他的粉丝。

170
00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:11.600
So I kind of geeked out when he finally got to direct an episode.
所以当他终于有机会执导一集时，我简直兴奋得像个狂热粉丝。

171
00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.860
But he directed a documentary called Spellbound.
他曾执导过一部名为《拼字比赛》的纪录片。

172
00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:20.780
It is a fantastic documentary about the Scripps National Spelling Bee.
这是一部关于全美斯克里普斯拼字比赛的精彩纪录片。

173
00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.460
And it follows eight of the young competitors.
它讲述了八位年轻参赛者的故事。

174
00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.360
It is wonderful.
它太棒了。

175
00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.900
So if you're looking for things to watch, watch Spellbound.
所以如果你在找好看的节目，去看《拼字比赛》吧。

176
00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.220
It is so good.
真的非常精彩。

177
00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.600
It was nominated for an Academy Award.
它曾获得过奥斯卡金像奖提名。

178
00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:33.500
Yes.
没错。

179
00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.140
Oh, my God.
天哪。

180
00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:34.900
I forgot that.
我都把这茬给忘了。

181
00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:35.180
Yes.
对的。

182
00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.040
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

183
00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.600
Well, we asked Jeff, how did you get this job?
嗯，我们问杰夫，你是怎么得到这份工作的？

184
00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.560
And I loved his answer.
我特别喜欢他的回答。

185
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.460
So, Sam, will you play that clip?
所以，萨姆，能放一下那个片段吗？

186
00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:53.420
When Greg was meeting people to talk about directing on the pilot, I got called in to meet with him.
当格雷格跟人开会商讨试播集导演的人选时，我被叫去见了他。

187
00:07:53.420 --> 00:08:10.140
He was flirting with the great and probably crazy idea to bring a true doc filmmaker on from the start to kind of overlay a more authentic doc style onto the show.
他当时正琢磨着一个很棒但可能也很疯狂的想法，那就是从一开始就引入真正的纪录片电影人，给节目叠加一种更真实的纪录片风格。

188
00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:15.000
I had just done my first feature doc, Spellbound, about kids in the National Spelling Bee.
我刚拍完我的第一部长篇纪录片《拼字比赛》，讲的是参加全国拼字比赛的孩子们。

189
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:25.000
And Greg thought the idea to have me on was an interesting one that he'd explore with NBC, who immediately said, not a chance.
格雷格觉得让我加入是个挺有意思的主意，他打算跟NBC探讨一下，结果NBC立马说：没门。

190
00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:31.940
I think it was almost two years later, I hadn't seen Greg at all, and I got a call out of the blue.
我想大概过了两年吧，我跟格雷格完全没联系，突然就接到了一个电话。

191
00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.500
Greg wanted to know now, would I like to work on the show?
格雷格现在想知道，我愿不愿意来节目里工作？

192
00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:41.760
At this point, he thought that he could talk NBC into it.
这时候，他觉得自己能说服NBC了。

193
00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:50.100
So, The Office Season 3, I had my first gig in the world of TV with the episode The Convict.
所以，在《办公室》第三季里，我迎来了自己在电视圈的第一份工作，就是执导《罪犯》这一集。

194
00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:57.540
Yeah, so this was his first scripted television show that he ever directed.
对，所以这也是他执导的有剧本电视剧的首秀。

195
00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:01.880
He was just coming out of the world of documentary, which I love.
他刚从纪录片领域转过来，我太喜欢这样了。

196
00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.260
I love that Greg did that, right?
我喜欢格雷格这么做，对吧？

197
00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:12.760
That he wanted a cinematographer who had shot documentaries, and now he wanted to hire a documentary film director.
他想要一个拍纪录片出身的摄影师，现在他又想雇佣一个纪录片电影导演。

198
00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:18.260
He was really interested in preserving the integrity of this documentary style for the show.
他真的很有兴趣为这部剧保持这种纪录片风格的完整性。

199
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.900
I also love that Greg is such a champion of people.
我也很喜欢格雷格特别支持和赏识人才。

200
00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:22.640
You know, he doesn't give up on you.
你知道的，他不会轻易放弃你。

201
00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:23.960
NBC said no.
NBC拒绝了。

202
00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.220
He was like, I'm going to get you in there, Jeff.
他当时说，杰夫，我一定把你弄进去。

203
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:26.780
You know?
你知道吗？

204
00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:27.080
Yeah.
对啊。

205
00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.120
And then he did.
然后他真的做到了。

206
00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:29.040
I just love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

207
00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:35.220
We also asked Jeff what it was like to shoot his first scripted television show, and here's what he had to say.
我们还问了杰夫，拍摄他的第一部电视剧是什么体验，以下是他的分享。

208
00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:43.280
The thing that stood out to me is that I had done all this prep work, figuring out all these shots.
最让我感触的是，我做了大量的前期准备工作，设计了各种镜头。

209
00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:54.300
And, you know, I just had a ton of thoughts about the way each line might be.
而且，你知道的，我对每一句台词的表现方式都有很多想法。

210
00:09:55.180 --> 00:10:04.980
And then when the shooting actually started, I realized that all the prep work I had done, it just didn't fit for the kind of show that this was.
但真的开拍时，我发现我之前所有的准备工作，根本不适合这种类型的剧。

211
00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:17.600
The first or second setup, I think, had me standing right by Pam's desk, and I realized that by then, all of the prep work I had done, it just didn't make any sense.
我记得在第一个或第二个机位设置时，我得站在帕姆的桌子旁边，然后我意识到，之前做的大部分准备工作全都没有意义了。

212
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:23.760
And I think that I just dropped all of it into the trash can right there.
我觉得我当时就把它们全都扔进垃圾桶了。

213
00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:29.540
Well, Angela, I remember Jeff standing at reception for that scene.
安吉拉，我记得杰夫那场戏就站在前台那儿。

214
00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:29.840
Yeah.
对啊。

215
00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.640
And we really bonded.
我们真的建立起了深厚的感情。

216
00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:38.340
I felt so fortunate that I got to have him up at reception with me because I just loved him instantly.
我觉得自己太幸运了，能让他在前台陪着我，因为我一眼就喜欢上了他。

217
00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.660
I feel like reception, you got that sometimes, like just sitting where you were sitting.
我觉得前台那边有时就是这样，就像你当时坐的位置一样。

218
00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:47.360
A lot of times that directors and writers would be sort of perched up there, either on that sofa.
很多时候导演和编剧都会坐在上面，要么就在那个沙发上。

219
00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.780
You know, they would sit on the sofa.
你知道的，他们会坐在沙发上。

220
00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:49.140
Yeah.
对啊。

221
00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.640
Right there and watch the scene.
就在那里看着拍戏。

222
00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.460
And I was a little jealous that you got to have all that time with them.
我当时还有点嫉妒你能跟他们相处那么长时间。

223
00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:59.800
Well, the other thing that used to happen at reception, though, Angela, is that people would stand like a wall in front of reception with their back to me.
不过安吉拉，前台以前经常发生的另一件事是，人们会像一堵墙一样站在前台前面，背对着我。

224
00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.920
And they would also steal my pens, and they would also leave their water bottles on the reception desk.
而且他们还会偷我的笔，把水瓶留在前台桌子上。

225
00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.280
So there's an upside and a downside.
所以有利也有弊吧。

226
00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.160
There was.
确实如此。

227
00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:07.900
There was.
确实如此。

228
00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:08.960
All right.
好了。

229
00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.440
Are you ready for Fast Fact No.
准备好听第三条速查事实了吗？

230
00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:10.780
3?
3？

231
00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:11.580
I am.
我已经准备好了。

232
00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.200
Fast Fact No.
速查事实第

233
00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:13.620
3.
3条。

234
00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:18.800
Wayne Wilderson, amazing comic actor, played Martin Nash.
韦恩·威尔德森，优秀的喜剧演员，饰演马丁·纳什。

235
00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:25.120
We also reached out to Wayne, and he sent in some audio clips about his time on the show.
我们也联系了韦恩，他发来了一些关于他在剧组经历的音频剪辑。

236
00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:25.900
He did.
他真的发了。

237
00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.180
Jenna, this time I was sliding into someone's DMs.
珍娜，这次我可是去私信联系别人了。

238
00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.420
Oh, I loved it.
哦，我太喜欢了。

239
00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.580
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

240
00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.640
I love that now you and I are just these two ladies in their 40s sliding into people's DMs.
我喜欢我们现在成了两个四十多岁、去私信别人的女士。

241
00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:37.820
I know, right?
对吧？

242
00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.200
Wayne is fantastic.
韦恩太棒了。

243
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.940
And we started by asking him how he came to be on The Office.
我们首先问他是怎么加入《办公室》的。

244
00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.200
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的讲述。

245
00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.240
Hey, guys.
大家好。

246
00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:46.920
It's Wayne here.
我是韦恩。

247
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:47.440
How are you doing?
你们过得怎么样？

248
00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:51.880
Thank you so much for letting me come to the party.
非常感谢让我来参加派对。

249
00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:52.620
This is great.
这太棒了。

250
00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.460
I dig the podcaSt.
我很喜欢这个播客。

251
00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.120
Okay.
好的。

252
00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.780
Jumping right into it.
我们马上开始。

253
00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:58.580
Question one.
第一个问题。

254
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.040
Can you share how you came to be on The Office?
你能分享一下你是怎么加入《办公室》的吗？

255
00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.240
Yeah.
好啊。

256
00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.840
I got to be on The Office.
我有幸参演了《办公室》。

257
00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:10.540
It was just a regular audition call.
这只是一次常规的试镜通知。

258
00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.560
They had this role.
他们当时有个角色。

259
00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.800
It was two episodes, working two different weeks.
总共两集，在两个不同的星期工作。

260
00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.540
And I already loved the show.
而且我本来就很喜欢这部剧。

261
00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.840
And I was a big fan of the British office.
我还是英版《办公室》的超级粉丝。

262
00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.020
So I was very excited for this audition.
所以我对这次试镜非常兴奋。

263
00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:32.380
Um, I knew Steve and I knew Adda just worked with those guys and Evan Almighty.
嗯，我认识史蒂夫，我也认识阿达，刚和他们合作过《冒牌天神》。

264
00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:38.300
Nancy, Steve's wife, is one of my oldest friends, but they swore they had nothing to do with getting the audition.
南希，也就是史蒂夫的妻子，是我最老的朋友之一，但他们发誓说这次试镜跟他们一点关系都没有。

265
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.720
So, that's what they said.
行吧，他们是这么说的。

266
00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:45.140
Uh, but I got the job and was super excited.
呃，不过我得到了这份工作，超级兴奋。

267
00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:55.000
In that particular episode, I'm not sure if I knew when I got the part that Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant had written it.
在那个特定的剧集里，我不确定当我得到角色时是否知道瑞克·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特是编剧。

268
00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:00.300
And I think those two episodes were the first ones that they ever did for the U.S.
而且我想那两集是他们为美版写的仅有的两集。

269
00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:01.200
office.
办公室。

270
00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.300
So, that was a, that was a bit of an honor.
所以，这，这算是一种荣幸。

271
00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.420
I did not know that he knew Nancy.
我不知道他认识南希。

272
00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.260
I didn't either, but it makes sense, right?
我也不知道，但这也说得通，对吧？

273
00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.580
I mean, they're both really funny, talented people.
我的意思是，他们都是非常搞笑、非常有才华的人。

274
00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:13.560
They were in Boston.
他们当时在波士顿。

275
00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

276
00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.220
I know.
我知道。

277
00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.740
I see them crossing paths.
我能想象他们的人生轨迹有交集。

278
00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:19.780
No, they have the comedy connection and the Boston connection.
不，他们有喜剧的联系和波士顿的联系。

279
00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.840
So, yeah, I guess that makes sense.
所以，好吧，我想这说得通。

280
00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:27.700
Well, you know, when we were trading emails with Wayne, too, we asked him if he still gets recognized for being on the office.
嗯，你知道的，当我们和韦恩互发邮件时，我们也问他是否还会因为演过《办公室》而被认出来。

281
00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:32.820
And he said yes all the time, especially now with the resurgence on Netflix.
他说经常被认出来，尤其是现在在Netflix上翻红之后。

282
00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.080
And he's so tickled by it, but he said it's all young people now.
他对此感到很高兴，但他说现在认出他的全都是年轻人。

283
00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:36.960
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

284
00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.900
I mean, we're crushing it with middle schoolers, guys.
我的意思是，我们在初中生里可是大受欢迎啊，伙计们。

285
00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:44.800
Because we talked about this on the merger, he had a big recurring on Veep as well.
因为我们在讨论《合并》那一集时提到，他在《副总统》里也有过重要的常驻角色。

286
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.580
But I think he gets recognized more for The Office, even though it was only two episodes.
但我认为他因为《办公室》而被认出的频率更高，尽管他只演了两集。

287
00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.560
Oh, Veep is so good.
噢，《副总统》太棒了。

288
00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.560
So good.
太棒了。

289
00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.960
You know, we exchanged a lot of emails with Wayne about this episode.
你知道的，我们关于这一集和韦恩交换了很多邮件。

290
00:13:55.060 --> 00:14:03.520
And we were talking about what it was like to rewatch this episode in light of everything that's happening in our country with the Black Lives Matter movement.
我们在讨论，鉴于我们国家正在发生的“黑人的命也是命”运动，重看这一集是什么感觉。

291
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.140
And here's what he had to say.
他是这么说的。

292
00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:06.080
Wow.
哇。

293
00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.720
I just watched it again.
我刚又看了一遍。

294
00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.600
I watch it, you know, maybe every year or so.
我大概每隔一年左右就会看一次。

295
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.500
So it's such a good episode.
所以这是一集非常棒的剧。

296
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:20.240
With everything that's going on in the world now, you know, it feels a little even edgier at some points.
结合现在世界上发生的一切，你知道，在某些地方感觉甚至更加尖锐了。

297
00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:33.240
But it's super poignant, I guess, for all the issues that we're dealing with now with race and how we deal with it and what's funny and what's not funny.
但我想，对于我们现在正在处理的所有关于种族的问题、我们如何处理这些问题、什么好笑什么不好笑，它都极其深刻。

298
00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:47.120
And who can say what, when, and, you know, this puts a magnifying glass on where we've been and how far we've come along, what comedy we can do.
以及谁能在什么时候说什么，你知道，这把放大镜对准了我们曾经的过往、我们取得了多大的进步，以及我们能做什么样的喜剧。

299
00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.180
So it was very interesting.
所以这非常有趣。

300
00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:53.220
I probably hadn't watched it in a year or so.
我大概有一年左右没看过它了。

301
00:14:53.220 --> 00:15:00.480
And to watch it during these times was very interesting.
在现在的时期看这部剧，真的很有意思。

302
00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:07.920
With that, the comedy and its commentary, I think it holds up very well.
结合它的喜剧效果和讽刺意味，我觉得它依然非常经久不衰。

303
00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.620
I think it's kind of a classic Office episode.
我觉得这可以说是《办公室》的一集经典剧集。

304
00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.280
I'm going to say it's a classic Office episode.
我敢说这就是一集经典的《办公室》。

305
00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.380
Boom.
砰。

306
00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:26.400
Well, Angela, I had not watched this episode since it aired, and I definitely found a new poignancy when I was watching it.
嗯，安吉拉，自从这集播出后我就没再看过，这次重看，我确实有了完全不同的感触。

307
00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:26.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，对啊。

308
00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:34.020
And there are definitely lines and moments that stood out to me, and I'll bring it up as we go through the episode.
确实有些台词和瞬间让我印象深刻，随着我们回顾这一集，我会慢慢提出来。

309
00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:34.600
Same.
我也是。

310
00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.120
Well, why don't we take a break?
那，我们为什么不先休息一下呢？

311
00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.840
And when we come back, we will break down the convict.
等我们回来，就会剖析《罪犯》这一集。

312
00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:39.940
We'll see ya.
回头见。

313
00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.410
Okay, so we are back.
好的，我们回来啦。

314
00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:56.050
Look, this episode starts with Hannah bringing her baby into the office.
听着，这一集的开场是汉娜把她的婴儿带到了办公室。

315
00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:00.630
She is setting up for her baby staying all day, clearly.
很显然，她正在为宝宝在这里待上一整天做准备。

316
00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:01.890
She's got a pack and play.
她带了一个便携婴儿床。

317
00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.570
Yeah, there's a pack and play.
对，有个便携婴儿床。

318
00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:07.070
I mean, she's moving in.
我的意思是，她这是要搬进来了。

319
00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:07.730
What's happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

320
00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:08.610
Yeah.
对啊。

321
00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:13.210
We had a fan question from Ellis Friedman, Victoria Leyva, and Megan Keel.
我们收到了来自埃利斯·弗里德曼、维多利亚·莱瓦和梅根·基尔的粉丝提问。

322
00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.950
Why did Hannah bring her baby into the office?
汉娜为什么要把她的宝宝带到办公室里？

323
00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.030
Yes, ladies.
是的，女士们。

324
00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:17.710
Why?
为什么呢？

325
00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.170
Why?
为什么呀？

326
00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.170
We don't know.
我们也不知道。

327
00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.050
I watched the deleted scenes.
我看了被删减的片段。

328
00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:24.590
I have a lot to bring to this episode that is explained in deleted scenes.
我为这一集准备了好多在删减片段里才解释过的内容。

329
00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.390
We'll get to that.
我们待会儿会聊到。

330
00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.770
This is not.
这个倒没有。

331
00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:30.850
There's a whole runner in the deleted scenes with the baby.
删减片段里其实有一整条关于这个婴儿的副线剧情。

332
00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.190
There's no explanation.
但根本没有任何解释。

333
00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.170
People holding the baby.
大家都在轮流抱孩子。

334
00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:34.850
Yeah.
是啊。

335
00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:43.750
I saw that in the script because I have the script for this one, and there are all these scenes of people with the baby, but never is it explained why the baby is there.
我在剧本里看到了，因为我有这一集的剧本，里面有所有大家和婴儿在一起的场景，但自始至终都没有解释过为什么要把孩子带来。

336
00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:53.490
I would like to point out that this is a very progressive choice by Michael to allow a new mother to bring their baby into the office for the day, so I appreciate that.
我想指出的是，迈克尔允许一位新妈妈把宝宝带到办公室呆上一天，这是一个非常开明的决定，所以我很赞赏这一点。

337
00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:59.710
Although what we didn't need him to do was get under the table and do an impression of Look Who's Talking.
不过，我们并不需要他钻到桌子底下模仿《看谁在说话》。

338
00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:04.410
Do you remember those movies with Kirstie Alley and John Travolta?
还记得柯茜·艾利和约翰·特拉沃尔塔演的那些电影吗？

339
00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.770
They were a huge hit.
它们当时可是超级大热门。

340
00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.870
Wait, is Bruce Willis the talking baby?
等等，那个会说话的婴儿是布鲁斯·威利斯配音的吗？

341
00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.130
Yeah, Bruce Willis.
对，布鲁斯·威利斯。

342
00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:19.670
So, Kirstie Alley has like a one-night stand with this cab driver played by John Travolta, and they have a baby, and now they have to figure out how to, I guess,
所以，柯茜·艾利和约翰·特拉沃尔塔饰演的出租车司机发生了一夜情，生了个孩子，现在他们不得不琢磨，我猜是……

343
00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.730
co-parent this baby when they're not a couple.
在不是情侣的情况下如何共同抚养这个孩子。

344
00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.650
Of course, spoiler alert, they're going to fall in love.
当然，剧透警告，他们最后会坠入爱河。

345
00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:25.310
Yay!
太棒了！

346
00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:36.230
But all the while, you're getting commentary on their parenting and their romance through the voice of the baby voiced by Bruce Willis.
但与此同时，你还能通过布鲁斯·威利斯配音的那个婴儿的声音，听到他们对育儿和浪漫关系的吐槽。

347
00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.110
As a grown man.
而且还是个成年男人的声音。

348
00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:41.990
So, because he's not doing a baby voice, he's a grown man voice and a baby voice.
所以，他配的不是婴儿的声音，而是成年男人的声音配上婴儿的视角。

349
00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.150
No, no, he's doing his own regular man voice.
不，不，他用的就是他平常成熟男人的声音。

350
00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:45.190
I want to be in that pitch meeting.
真想去旁听一下那个电影创意的提案会议。

351
00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:47.050
I want to be in that pitch meeting.
真想去旁听那个提案会议。

352
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.950
I want to see the person that's like, here's the thing.
真想见见那个提出这种创意的人。

353
00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.430
The baby talks, and it's Bruce Willis.
婴儿会说话，而且是布鲁斯·威利斯的声音。

354
00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:58.470
The same guy that said, yippee-ki-yay, mother-effer, is going to be the baby.
那个说过“圣诞快乐，混蛋”的硬汉，居然要来演个婴儿。

355
00:17:58.610 --> 00:17:59.590
It's going to be great.
这绝对会很棒。

356
00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.270
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

357
00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:04.250
Okay, well, in the deleted scenes, there is a baby runner.
好吧，在删减片段里，有一个关于婴儿的支线。

358
00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:09.150
I mean, Karen holds the baby and flirts with Jim, and Pam watches it all.
我是说，凯伦抱着婴儿跟吉姆调情，彭世看在眼里。

359
00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.790
I read that in the script.
我在剧本里读到过这个。

360
00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:11.550
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

361
00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:16.530
Kelly holds the baby and just jiggles it in front of Ryan, and Ryan finally is like, what, Kelly?
凯利抱着婴儿在瑞恩面前晃悠，瑞恩最后终于忍不住说，干嘛，凯利？

362
00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:17.170
What?
干嘛？

363
00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.870
Are you holding a baby because you want me to want to have a baby with you?
你抱着个孩子是因为想让我跟你生个孩子吗？

364
00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.390
And she's like, no, what are you talking about?
然后她说，没有啊，你在说什么呢？

365
00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:22.670
Whatever.
随便吧。

366
00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:26.030
And then three seconds later, she's like, oh, my God, I want a baby right now.
结果三秒钟后，她就说，天呐，我现在就想要个孩子。

367
00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:28.390
It's actually really funny.
其实真的挺搞笑的。

368
00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:32.470
And then there's a very funny deleted scene where Andy and Dwight have like a baby off.
然后还有一个超级好笑的删减片段，安迪和德怀特搞了一场类似比谁更像婴儿的较量。

369
00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.770
Like, they're so ridiculous.
真的太荒谬了。

370
00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:35.210
These two are so ridiculous.
这两个家伙太荒谬了。

371
00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:37.790
Like, Andy's like, I was a baby model.
就像安迪说的，我当过婴儿模特。

372
00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.110
Not going to apologize for it.
我才不为此道歉呢。

373
00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.550
I was a beautiful baby, and I modeled.
我曾经是个漂亮的婴儿，我还当过模特。

374
00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:46.130
This is like their whole competition in the last episode about who has seen more movies.
这就像他们在上一集里争论谁看过更多电影的那场全方位比赛一样。

375
00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:47.090
Exactly.
完全正确。

376
00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.910
So they're arguing about themselves as babies.
所以他们是在争论自己当婴儿时的经历。

377
00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:53.490
Andy was, I guess, a gorgeous baby and modeled.
我猜安迪以前是个漂亮宝宝，还当过模特。

378
00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:59.030
And Dwight was like, well, I weighed 13 pounds, and my mom couldn't walk for three months.
而德怀特则说，我生下来有13磅重，我妈三个月下不了地。

379
00:18:59.150 --> 00:18:59.810
So take that.
怎么样，厉害吧。

380
00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:01.130
It's so weird.
真是太怪了。

381
00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:01.750
All right.
好吧。

382
00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:06.910
Well, the scene with Pam having to watch Jim and Karen fuss over this baby was deleted.
总之，彭被迫看着吉姆和凯伦围着这个婴儿嘘寒问暖的那场戏被删掉了。

383
00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:12.490
But the next scene in the episode is Pam watching Jim and Karen kind of flirt at the copy machine.
但剧集里的下一场戏是彭看着吉姆和凯伦在复印机旁打情骂俏。

384
00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:13.470
Yeah.
对啊。

385
00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:20.250
And at 1 minute 47 seconds, you can still see my zit from the week before.
在1分47秒的时候，你依然能看到我前一周长的那颗痘痘。

386
00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:21.570
Stop it.
别说了。

387
00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:23.370
From the merger.
就公司合并时期那颗。

388
00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.710
It's a little smaller, but it's still there.
小了一点，但还在。

389
00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.930
You have got to stop pointing it out.
你非得把这事指出来不可吗。

390
00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:28.850
None of us noticed.
我们谁都没注意到。

391
00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:32.610
Or maybe Hadley did, because I know she noticed Dwight's zit.
或者也许哈德利注意到了，因为我知道她注意到了德怀特的痘痘。

392
00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:35.650
But Jenna, you like to track things.
不过珍娜，你很喜欢记录这些。

393
00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.430
Stop tracking your acne.
别老盯着你的青春痘不放了。

394
00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.490
Well, I think my zit's going to be gone next week.
好吧，我觉得我的痘痘下周就会消下去了。

395
00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.350
But I mean, we'll see.
不过呢，走着瞧吧。

396
00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:43.510
We'll see.
走着瞧。

397
00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:45.050
It'll make your list, I'm sure.
我敢肯定它会上你的黑名单的。

398
00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:46.310
All right.
好吧。

399
00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:48.570
So then we have this, you know, Jim talking head.
接下来我们有这个，你知道的，吉姆的单人采访。

400
00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:51.070
And he says that he is seeing Karen.
他说他正在和凯伦交往。

401
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:51.670
He is.
他是。

402
00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.390
He admits it.
他承认了。

403
00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:56.910
But he isn't ready to talk about it openly, because he doesn't want some people, you know,
但他还没准备好公开谈论这件事，因为他不想让某些人，你知道的，

404
00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:57.830
treating them differently.
对他们另眼相看。

405
00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.830
I have a beef with Jim.
我对吉姆有意见。

406
00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.790
I just wrote, not cool.
我刚写了，太逊了。

407
00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:03.170
Not cool.
太逊了。

408
00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:04.090
Yeah.
是啊。

409
00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.110
This goes back to my wishy-washy Jim.
这又得扯回我那个优柔寡断的吉姆了。

410
00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:08.150
Yeah.
是啊。

411
00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:09.190
Wishy-washy Jim.
优柔寡断的吉姆。

412
00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.290
There it is again.
又来了。

413
00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:11.050
All right.
好吧。

414
00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.430
So now we move into the conference room.
所以现在我们进入会议室。

415
00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.890
We've got Angela, Kevin, Michael, and Pam.
里面有安吉拉、凯文、迈克尔和帕姆。

416
00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.890
They are all on the speakerphone to Jan.
他们都在开免提跟简通话。

417
00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:21.470
And they are discussing this mysterious check that has arrived.
他们在讨论这张寄来的神秘支票。

418
00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:22.310
Yeah.
是啊。

419
00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:23.310
I have a question, Jenna.
我有个问题，珍娜。

420
00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:23.650
Yeah.
说吧。

421
00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.150
I get why Michael's on the phone.
我明白为什么迈克尔在电话里。

422
00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.650
I get why the accountants are.
我也明白为什么会计们在。

423
00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.430
Why is Pam there?
为什么帕姆也在？

424
00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:30.670
Is it just because Michael just likes to have Pam around?
难道只是因为迈克尔喜欢让帕姆在身边？

425
00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.090
She's like keeper of the minutes or something.
她就像是会议记录员什么的。

426
00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:33.850
Yeah.
是啊。

427
00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:36.550
He sees Pam as his personal assistant.
他把帕姆当成他的私人助理。

428
00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.790
She is not his personal assistant.
她才不是他的私人助理。

429
00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:43.690
She is the receptionist, but he doesn't have a personal assistant.
她是前台，但他没有私人助理。

430
00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:47.490
And so he sort of, you know, makes her play that role.
所以他差不多就是，你知道的，让她扮演那个角色。

431
00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:48.070
Yeah.
是啊。

432
00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.630
She's always in these meetings she shouldn't be in.
她总是在开那些她根本不该参加的会。

433
00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:51.090
That's right.
没错。

434
00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:51.470
Always.
总是这样。

435
00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:56.270
There's many episodes of meetings of Pam in conversations between Michael and Jan.
有很多集里，帕姆都会出席迈克尔和简的谈话会议。

436
00:20:56.770 --> 00:21:00.970
And I love it because the camera will just like pan mid scene.
而且我超喜欢，因为镜头会在中途突然摇过去。

437
00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.470
And then it reveals Pam has been sitting there with a notebook the whole time.
然后就会发现帕姆其实一直坐在那里拿着个笔记本。

438
00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:06.230
I mean, she's always in these scenes.
我是说，她总是在这些场景里。

439
00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:06.950
So awkward.
太尴尬了。

440
00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:07.710
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

441
00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:08.690
As an actress.
作为一名演员。

442
00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:09.650
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

443
00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:10.270
I bet.
我敢说。

444
00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:17.750
Jan eventually explains that this check is something that they're getting in exchange for hiring an ex-convict.
简最后解释说，这张支票是他们雇佣前囚犯所获得的补贴。

445
00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:22.370
Which Michael is like, I didn't hire an ex-convict.
对此迈克尔的反应是，我没雇佣过前囚犯啊。

446
00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:32.690
They come to realize that one of the Stanford transfers must be part of this program, meaning that there is someone from Stanford who has a criminal record.
