出演过《摩登家庭》的埃里克·斯通斯特里特在这则广告里饰演一个呕吐的员工。

903
00:42:12.230 --> 00:42:13.630
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

904
00:42:13.850 --> 00:42:14.410
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

905
00:42:14.510 --> 00:42:15.190
That's amazing.
太绝了。

906
00:42:15.950 --> 00:42:16.150
All right.
好吧。

907
00:42:16.250 --> 00:42:21.870
So also in the scene, after Michael announces to the entire office that Martin is an ex-convict,
所以在这场戏里，迈克尔向整个办公室宣布马丁是个前科犯之后，

908
00:42:22.090 --> 00:42:30.270
he then challenges everyone to name a white man they trust, and he will name a black man he trusts even more.
接着他向所有人发出挑战，说出一个他们信任的白人，他就会说出一个他更信任的黑人。

909
00:42:30.610 --> 00:42:33.690
So he's like, Pam, name a white man you truSt.
所以他就说，帕姆，说出一个你信任的白人。

910
00:42:33.830 --> 00:42:35.830
And she says, my dad.
然后她说，我爸爸。

911
00:42:36.410 --> 00:42:38.690
And he says, Danny Glover.
然后他说，丹尼·格洛弗。

912
00:42:38.890 --> 00:42:42.130
In the script, there is a Martin talking head.
在剧本里，有一个马丁的单采镜头。

913
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:46.870
And I don't know if this is in the deleted scenes, Angela, but it made me laugh out loud.
我不知道这算不算在删减片段里，安吉拉，但这让我笑出了声。

914
00:42:47.030 --> 00:42:48.290
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

915
00:42:48.770 --> 00:42:51.950
Martin says, Michael's an all right guy.
马丁说，迈克尔是个不错的人。

916
00:42:52.450 --> 00:42:57.790
He told me he trusts me more than Kirsten Dunst, and no one's ever told me that before.
他告诉我他对我的信任甚至超过了克尔斯滕·邓斯特，以前从来没有人对我说过这种话。

917
00:42:58.030 --> 00:42:59.630
I love that talking head so much.
我太喜欢那个单采镜头了。

918
00:42:59.630 --> 00:43:03.350
It is three sentences, but it is so rich with information.
虽然只有三句话，但信息量太丰富了。

919
00:43:04.250 --> 00:43:06.410
And was that in the deleted scenes?
那段在删减片段里吗？

920
00:43:06.530 --> 00:43:08.350
Can I see that talking head or no?
我能看那个单采镜头吗，还是不能？

921
00:43:08.550 --> 00:43:10.210
No, it's not in the deleted scenes.
不，它不在删减片段里。

922
00:43:10.230 --> 00:43:11.110
And I'm really sad.
我真的好难过。

923
00:43:11.330 --> 00:43:14.990
There is a Martin talking head in the deleted scenes, and it's this one.
删减片段里确实有一个马丁的单采镜头，就是这个。

924
00:43:15.110 --> 00:43:20.670
He says, usually when people find out about the prison thing, yeah, they get pretty weird.
他说，通常当人们发现坐牢这事时，对，他们就会变得很怪异。

925
00:43:21.110 --> 00:43:21.970
That's a good one.
这个挺搞笑的。

926
00:43:22.290 --> 00:43:27.570
All right, Jenna, now we're in the break room, and we find out why Martin went to prison.
好了，珍娜，现在我们来到茶水间，我们知道了马丁为什么要进监狱。

927
00:43:27.570 --> 00:43:31.970
Yes, Martin says, do you guys want to know what I was in for?
对，马丁说，你们想知道我是因为什么进去的吗？

928
00:43:32.150 --> 00:43:35.850
And he explains that he went to prison for insider trading.
然后他解释说他是因为内幕交易进了监狱。

929
00:43:36.230 --> 00:43:39.930
Now we move into a Kevin talking head that I love.
现在我们来到凯文的一个单采镜头，我超爱这个。

930
00:43:40.270 --> 00:43:42.130
I laughed out loud.
我笑出声来。

931
00:43:42.290 --> 00:43:52.070
He says, I asked Martin to explain why he went to jail three times, because it sounds a lot like what I do every day here at the office.
他说，我让马丁解释了三次他为什么进局子，因为这听起来太像我每天在办公室里做的事了。

932
00:43:52.070 --> 00:43:58.370
Yes, Jenna, there's a whole theory online that Dunder Mifflin is a front, like a money laundering front.
对的，珍娜，网上流传着一种阴谋论，说邓德米夫林是个空壳，比如洗钱空壳公司。

933
00:43:59.270 --> 00:44:00.830
Yes, there is.
没错，确实有。

934
00:44:01.090 --> 00:44:02.030
There is.
有的。

935
00:44:02.230 --> 00:44:05.870
And that maybe Kevin and I and the accountants are in on it.
而且也许我和凯文还有会计们都参与其中。

936
00:44:06.010 --> 00:44:09.190
So here's a fan question from Thomas O'Brien.
所以这里有一个来自托马斯·奥布莱恩的粉丝提问。

937
00:44:09.190 --> 00:44:12.450
And he he says that he knows about this theory.
他说他知道这个理论。

938
00:44:12.850 --> 00:44:21.470
And the main reason for this is that Scranton consistently outperforms all the other branches, despite the rapidly decreasing paper market.
主要原因在于，尽管纸张市场急剧萎缩，但斯克兰顿分公司的业绩一直压倒所有其他分公司。

939
00:44:21.710 --> 00:44:24.950
And Thomas wants to know, what do we think about this theory?
托马斯想知道，我们对这个理论怎么看？

940
00:44:25.330 --> 00:44:30.830
Do we think it has any merit that Dunder Mifflin is actually a front for money laundering?
我们觉得邓德米夫林实际上是洗钱空壳公司这种说法有道理吗？

941
00:44:30.830 --> 00:44:35.750
I would say no, I don't think it really is a front for money laundering.
我想说没有，我不觉得它真的是个洗钱空壳公司。

942
00:44:35.930 --> 00:44:44.450
I mean, if that was a part of the story, I believe Greg Daniels would have revealed that to us in the finale or somewhere in the last season.
我的意思是，如果那是故事的一部分，我相信格雷格·丹尼尔斯会在大结局或者最后一季的某个地方向我们揭晓的。

943
00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:47.290
So no, but I am curious.
所以并没有，不过我挺好奇的。

944
00:44:47.750 --> 00:44:54.150
It does sound like Kevin is participating in some sort of something shady.
这听起来确实像是凯文在参与某种见不得光的事情。

945
00:44:54.410 --> 00:44:55.150
Yeah, right.
对，没错。

946
00:44:55.230 --> 00:44:55.910
Because that's what it is.
因为事情本来就是这样。

947
00:44:56.010 --> 00:44:56.850
It's insider trading.
这是内幕交易。

948
00:44:57.030 --> 00:44:58.070
It's not money laundering.
不是洗钱。

949
00:44:58.310 --> 00:45:00.170
Martin didn't go to prison for money laundering.
马丁不是因为洗钱进的监狱。

950
00:45:00.170 --> 00:45:01.870
He went to prison for insider trading.
他是因为内幕交易进的监狱。

951
00:45:02.070 --> 00:45:02.430
I know.
我知道。

952
00:45:02.510 --> 00:45:05.890
But this is the theory online that Dunder Mifflin is a front for money laundering.
但网上有一种理论，说邓德米夫林其实是个洗钱的幌子。

953
00:45:06.290 --> 00:45:09.110
And I'm going to say I could see it.
而且我打算说，我能理解。

954
00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:11.290
Oh, no, I could see it.
哦，不，我真的能理解。

955
00:45:11.510 --> 00:45:19.170
I could see it because if you were going to have a money laundering front, by the way, I've also been watching a lot of Ozark and that's all he does.
我能理解，因为顺便说一句，如果你要找个洗钱的幌子——我最近也看了很多《黑钱胜地》，那剧里他整天就干这个。

956
00:45:19.590 --> 00:45:24.470
If you watch Ozark, he has to launder money for the drug cartel.
如果你看过《黑钱胜地》，他必须得为贩毒集团洗钱。

957
00:45:24.590 --> 00:45:27.270
So I'm like, oh, my gosh, yes, a paper company.
所以我就想，哦天哪，没错，一家造纸公司。

958
00:45:27.270 --> 00:45:29.730
And you have to you have like all this inventory.
而且你还得有各种各样的库存。

959
00:45:29.730 --> 00:45:34.730
And then you have sort of like a boss who's kind of incompetent who might not catch everything.
然后你还有一个有点无能、可能不会注意到所有事情的老板。

960
00:45:35.110 --> 00:45:35.550
Right.
没错。

961
00:45:35.550 --> 00:45:38.050
I think I I can see it, Thomas.
我觉得我能理解，托马斯。

962
00:45:38.270 --> 00:45:38.950
I can see it.
我能理解。

963
00:45:38.950 --> 00:45:40.890
But I'm also watching Ozark.
不过我也在看《黑钱胜地》。

964
00:45:41.050 --> 00:45:42.450
So maybe that's informing me.
所以可能受了点影响。

965
00:45:42.910 --> 00:45:43.250
All right.
好吧。

966
00:45:43.590 --> 00:45:49.170
Well, in this scene, Martin fields a lot of questions from all of us about what prison was like.
嗯，在这个场景里，马丁回答了我们大家提出的许多关于监狱生活是什么样的问题。

967
00:45:49.290 --> 00:45:53.910
And he gives a rather sort of rosy view of prison.
他对监狱生活给出了一种相当美好的看法。

968
00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:56.210
He's like, oh, yeah, we had outside time.
他说，哦，对啊，我们有户外活动时间。

969
00:45:56.250 --> 00:45:57.830
We got to watch TV.
我们能看电视。

970
00:45:58.410 --> 00:46:00.510
I got to take some classes.
我还能上几门课。

971
00:46:00.990 --> 00:46:03.590
Pam's like they had watercolor classes in prison.
帕姆就说，监狱里居然还有水彩画课。

972
00:46:03.590 --> 00:46:08.550
And then we're like, wow, Michael, it sounds like prison is better than Dunder Mifflin.
然后我们就说，哇，迈克尔，听起来监狱比邓德米夫林还要好。

973
00:46:08.690 --> 00:46:09.810
We're kind of teasing Michael.
我们有点在逗迈克尔。

974
00:46:09.970 --> 00:46:10.110
Right.
对吧。

975
00:46:10.290 --> 00:46:16.230
And then Michael is just very upset at this implication that Dunder Mifflin is worse than prison.
然后迈克尔对这种“邓德米夫林比监狱还不如”的暗示感到非常难过。

976
00:46:16.410 --> 00:46:20.770
What you have to remember is that everyone at Dunder Mifflin is Michael's family.
你必须记住的是，邓德米夫林的每个人都是迈克尔的家人。

977
00:46:21.030 --> 00:46:23.330
And Dunder Mifflin is like his home away from home.
而邓德米夫林就像是他的第二个家。

978
00:46:23.510 --> 00:46:28.390
So basically, his family has just told him that prison is better than home.
所以基本上，他的家人刚刚告诉他，监狱比家还要好。

979
00:46:28.710 --> 00:46:28.850
Yeah.
是啊。

980
00:46:28.990 --> 00:46:32.450
Prison is better than than this world that that they've made together.
监狱比他们一起创造的这个世界还要好。

981
00:46:32.450 --> 00:46:34.270
And so Michael is really hurt.
所以迈克尔真的很受伤。

982
00:46:34.510 --> 00:46:37.570
Michael had no issue with Martin until right now.
迈克尔直到刚才对马丁都没有任何意见。

983
00:46:37.710 --> 00:46:46.970
And it's because, you know, somehow his his employees, which are like his family, think that there's some other cooler place to be.
那是因为，你知道的，不知怎么的，他的员工——就像他的家人一样——觉得还有什么其他更酷的地方可去。

984
00:46:47.150 --> 00:46:49.590
And he's like, no, this is the best place to be.
而他就觉得，不，这里才是最好的地方。

985
00:46:49.710 --> 00:46:51.630
You guys, we have it amazing here.
伙计们，我们在这里过得太棒了。

986
00:46:51.730 --> 00:46:55.670
And he can't believe that they can't see Dunder Mifflin the way he can.
他简直不敢相信他们看不到邓德米夫林的好，就像他看不到一样。

987
00:46:55.810 --> 00:47:02.030
Well, I asked Wayne what it was like to shoot that break room scene because here he was.
嗯，我问韦恩拍摄那个茶水间场景是什么感觉，因为当时他在那儿。

988
00:47:02.030 --> 00:47:05.730
He was a guest star and he had to really drive that scene, you know?
他是一个客串演员，而且他得撑起那个场景，你知道吗？

989
00:47:05.970 --> 00:47:06.110
Yeah.
对。

990
00:47:06.350 --> 00:47:12.470
And I mean, I remember what it was like to be a guest actor on shows and how intimidating something like that could be.
我的意思是，我记得在节目中当客串演员是什么感觉，那种事情会有多吓人。

991
00:47:12.670 --> 00:47:15.970
And so I just wanted to hear what was it like to do this scene from his perspective.
所以我只是想听听，从他的角度来看，拍这个场景是什么感觉。

992
00:47:16.270 --> 00:47:17.250
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

993
00:47:17.250 --> 00:47:35.370
Coming to work on your guys' awesome show, it wasn't, even though the show was so huge, it wasn't intimidating just because everybody was having like Christmas morning fun.
来到你们这个超棒的节目工作，虽然节目非常火爆，但一点也不吓人，因为每个人都像是在过圣诞节早上一样开心。

994
00:47:35.370 --> 00:47:38.270
Like they couldn't believe their good fortune.
就像他们不敢相信自己的好运气一样。

995
00:47:38.410 --> 00:47:44.290
They couldn't believe the people they got to work with, both in front and behind the camera.
他们不敢相信自己能跟镜头前后的这些人一起工作。

996
00:47:44.910 --> 00:47:48.530
And they couldn't believe how funny the writing was.
而且他们不敢相信剧本写得这么搞笑。

997
00:47:50.930 --> 00:47:54.890
So that scene was, I loved that scene.
所以那个场景，我太喜欢那个场景了。

998
00:47:54.890 --> 00:48:05.070
And I love sort of being the fish out of water, getting into the water so everybody can get out of the pool, if that makes any sense.
我喜欢那种格格不入的感觉，跳进水里让大家都从泳池里出来，如果这还算讲得通的话。

999
00:48:05.070 --> 00:48:06.430
I don't really know what I'm talking about.
我其实不知道自己在说些什么。

1000
00:48:07.510 --> 00:48:14.070
But yeah, it was an easy environment to do your best work.
不过是的，那是一个很容易发挥出你最佳水平的环境。

1001
00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:23.650
So yeah, that's, I knew that day like, oh, got to redo my reel because that's the shizzle.
所以，对，那天我就知道，哦，我得重新剪辑我的短片了，因为那太绝了。

1002
00:48:25.070 --> 00:48:26.990
But I thought that was the sweetest response.
但我觉得那是超级贴心的回应。

1003
00:48:27.650 --> 00:48:29.990
All right, Jenna, I have something to say to you.
好吧，珍娜，我有话对你说。

1004
00:48:30.350 --> 00:48:30.490
What?
什么？

1005
00:48:30.870 --> 00:48:32.270
Pam-a-lemma-ding-dong.
帕姆—阿—莱玛—叮—咚。

1006
00:48:32.610 --> 00:48:33.110
Oh, boy.
噢，天哪。

1007
00:48:33.530 --> 00:48:33.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1008
00:48:34.350 --> 00:48:36.830
So it's 10 minutes, 38 seconds.
所以这段有10分38秒。

1009
00:48:37.010 --> 00:48:40.490
And Andy is hitting on Pam in all the wrong ways.
而且安迪用各种极其不对劲的方式在撩帕姆。

1010
00:48:40.690 --> 00:48:40.990
No.
不会吧。

1011
00:48:41.210 --> 00:48:43.710
And the look on Jim's face, it says it all.
吉姆脸上的表情，一切尽在不言中。

1012
00:48:43.830 --> 00:48:45.030
This is a great prank.
这是一个绝妙的恶作剧。

1013
00:48:45.270 --> 00:48:46.390
It's going great.
进展非常顺利。

1014
00:48:46.650 --> 00:48:52.250
And then we have the talking head from Pam where she's like, that was, wow.
然后是帕姆的单人采访，她大概是说，那个，哇。

1015
00:48:53.410 --> 00:48:55.070
So she loves this prank.
所以她很喜欢这个恶作剧。

1016
00:48:55.270 --> 00:48:56.070
She's into it.
她很受用。

1017
00:48:56.530 --> 00:49:01.610
Well, she's impressed at Jim's ability to prank her in this way.
嗯，她对吉姆能用这种方式对她恶作剧感到印象深刻。

1018
00:49:01.730 --> 00:49:03.790
I think she's like, wow, I see where you're going.
我觉得她心里在想，哇，我懂你的意思了。

1019
00:49:04.030 --> 00:49:07.830
Now, Jenna, there is a deleted scene where Pam gets him back.
话说，珍娜，有一个被删掉的片段是帕姆反击了。

1020
00:49:08.050 --> 00:49:09.550
Yes, that is in the script.
对，剧本里是有的。

1021
00:49:09.830 --> 00:49:12.650
This is a portion of this story that got cut out.
这是后来被剪掉的故事的一部分。

1022
00:49:12.990 --> 00:49:16.250
There's a bit of a prank war that happens, right?
算是爆发了一场恶作剧大战，对吧？

1023
00:49:16.250 --> 00:49:17.530
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1024
00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:24.030
So Pam gives Andy all this information about all these things that would just be a horrible
所以帕姆把所有这些信息都告诉了安迪，全都是那些会让吉姆觉得糟糕透顶的

1025
00:49:24.030 --> 00:49:28.390
night out for Jim, like drinking white Russians, like just going out.
夜晚活动，比如喝白俄鸡尾酒，纯粹就是出去浪。

1026
00:49:28.570 --> 00:49:28.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1027
00:49:29.110 --> 00:49:30.530
Going to this German restaurant.
去那家德国餐厅。

1028
00:49:31.450 --> 00:49:33.790
She basically is like, you know what, Andy?
她基本上就是说，你知道吗，安迪？

1029
00:49:34.770 --> 00:49:37.770
I'm not available, but Jim would love to hang out.
我没空，不过吉姆很想出去玩。

1030
00:49:37.950 --> 00:49:39.470
He would love a buddy.
他很想找个伴儿。

1031
00:49:39.770 --> 00:49:39.930
Yeah.
对。

1032
00:49:40.250 --> 00:49:41.910
And so Andy's like, what are you doing tonight?
于是安迪就说，你今晚干嘛呢？

1033
00:49:42.030 --> 00:49:42.790
We're going out.
我们出去。

1034
00:49:42.910 --> 00:49:44.170
And Jim's like, whoa, whoa, whoa, wait, wait.
然后吉姆就说，哇，哇，哇，等等，等等。

1035
00:49:44.170 --> 00:49:44.220
Right.
没错。

1036
00:49:44.390 --> 00:49:46.230
So she does get him back.
所以她确实反击了。

1037
00:49:46.390 --> 00:49:47.090
She does.
她确实反击了。

1038
00:49:47.230 --> 00:49:50.650
But that did not end up in the episode, which I think is a little bit unfortunate
但那段最后没有出现在正片里，我觉得有点可惜

